  "notes": "Sahara International Petrochemical Company (SIPCHEM; ticker 2310) audited consolidated financial statements for the year ended 31 December 2025 with FY2024 comparatives, from the full audited PDF in the 'Annual / 2025' cell of the Saudi Exchange company-profile 'Financial Statements' tab (Resources/fsPdf/411_0_2026-03-27...). Auditor PwC. Board authorised issuance on 27 Ramadan 1447H / 16 March 2026 (used as filed_at). The filed PDF is digital text throughout (single-column layout, transcribed from the text layer). Amounts are in thousands of Saudi Riyals (scale 1000). FY2025 was a LOSS year: SIPCHEM reported a net loss of SAR 772.4m as petrochemical margins compressed (gross profit collapsed to SAR 256.7m from SAR 1,439.5m) and it booked a SAR 300m impairment of property, plant and equipment; retained earnings fell to SAR 2.7bn. net_income, net_income_parent and comprehensive_income are all negative for 2025. income_taxes_and_zakat sums the reported 'Zakat (expense) / credit', 'Income tax expense' and 'Deferred tax credit / (expense)' lines (also carried split); in FY2024 this is a net +18.2m credit (a zakat credit exceeded the tax charges), which trips the effective-tax plausibility bound as a warn - expected. operating_income is the reported 'Operating (loss) / profit'. impairment_charges is the 'Impairment of property, plant and equipment' add-back on the cash-flow statement. additional_paid_in_capital is 'Share premium'; other_reserves is the reported 'Other reserves' (hedge / FVOCI / translation). long_term_debt is 'Long term borrowings' (non-current); current_debt sums 'Current portion of long term borrowings' and 'Short term borrowings'. IFRS 16 lease liabilities are mapped separately. defined_benefit_obligation is the non-current 'Employees' benefits'. investments_associates is 'Investments in equity accounted investees'. depreciation_amortization sums 'Depreciation of property, plant and equipment and right of use assets' and 'Amortization of intangible assets and long term prepaid employees' benefits' from the cash-flow statement. capex is 'Payments for purchase of property, plant and equipment'. interest_paid is 'Finance costs paid'; zakat_paid is 'Zakat and income tax paid'; dividends_paid is the shareholder dividend (NCI dividends of SAR 122,250 thousand excluded). The cash-flow statement reconciles with a separate 'Effect of exchange rate fluctuations' line. Statement page references are the printed page numbers: financial position 7-8, profit or loss 9, comprehensive income 10, changes in equity 11-12, cash flows 13-14.",
